CHUNK({"chunk":"Q","module":"m4","topics":[{"id":"m4-sustainable-development","title":"Sustainable development and the origin of the SDGs","short":"Sustainable development","blurb":"The meaning of sustainable development, its limits, poverty and equity, how the SDGs grew from Johannesburg and Rio+20, and why environment and development go together.","source":"Lecture W4 (Sustainable Development Goals), pages 1, 3–4","tabs":[{"title":"Meaning","html":"\n          <p class=\"lead\"><b>Sustainable development</b> meets the needs of the present <b>without compromising the ability of future generations</b> to meet their own needs.</p>\n          <ul>\n            <li><b>Limits</b>: not absolute; set by technology, social organisation, biosphere's absorbing capacity; can be improved.</li>\n            <li><b>Poverty</b>: not inevitable; endemic poverty invites ecological disasters; meet basic needs.</li>\n            <li><b>Equity</b>: fair share for the poor; citizen participation, international democracy.</li>\n            <li>The <b>affluent</b> live within ecological means (e.g. energy).</li>\n            <li><b>Population</b> matched to ecosystem's productive potential.</li>\n          </ul>\n          <div class=\"note exam\"><b>Not a fixed state of harmony</b> but a <b>process of change</b> (resources, investment, technology, institutions); painful choices.</div>\n        "},{"title":"Genesis of SDGs","html":"\n          <ol class=\"steps\">\n            <li><b>World Summit on Sustainable Development, Johannesburg</b>: renewed commitment through the <b>Johannesburg Plan of Implementation (JPOI)</b>.</li>\n            <li><b>2012</b>: outcome document <b>\"The Future We Want\"</b>: SDGs to build on <b>Agenda 21</b> and JPOI; Commission for Sustainable Development replaced by a <b>high-level political forum</b>.</li>\n            <li><b>September 2015</b>: SDGs agreed at the <b>United Nations, New York</b>.</li>\n          </ol>\n        "},{"title":"Environment and awareness","html":"\n          <p>Development and environmental management: <b>two sides of one agenda</b>.</p>\n          <p><b>Awareness</b>: conservation is everyone's responsibility; India needs nationwide awareness.</p>\n          <ul>\n            <li>Causes of ignorance: <b>illiteracy</b>, poorly trained officials/leaders, no organised education effort.</li>\n            <li>Key areas: <b>agriculture, industry and health</b>.</li>\n            <li>Channels: formal education, non-formal adult education, training officials/opinion leaders, <b>mass media</b>.</li>\n            <li>People should <b>seek</b> knowledge.</li>\n          </ul>\n        "}],"flashcards":[{"front":"Define sustainable development.","back":"Meeting present needs without compromising future generations' ability to meet theirs."},{"front":"Are the limits of sustainable development absolute?","back":"<b>No</b>; set by current technology, social organisation and the biosphere's absorbing capacity."},{"front":"What was \"The Future We Want\"?","back":"The <b>2012</b> outcome document that committed states to build the SDGs."}],"cardCount":6,"formulaCount":0},{"id":"m4-sdgs","title":"The 17 Sustainable Development Goals","short":"The 17 SDGs","blurb":"All seventeen goals with their full aims, grouped so they are easier to remember.","source":"Lecture W4 (Sustainable Development Goals), page 2","tabs":[{"title":"Goals 1–9","html":"\n          <table class=\"tbl\">\n            <tbody>\n              <tr><td><b>1</b></td><td>End <b>poverty</b> in all its forms everywhere</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>2</b></td><td>End <b>hunger</b>, food security, better nutrition, sustainable agriculture</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>3</b></td><td>Healthy lives and <b>well-being</b> for all at all ages</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>4</b></td><td>Inclusive, equitable quality <b>education</b>, lifelong learning</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>5</b></td><td><b>Gender equality</b>, empower all women and girls</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>6</b></td><td>Clean <b>water and sanitation</b> for all</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>7</b></td><td>Affordable, reliable, sustainable, modern <b>energy</b> for all</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>8</b></td><td>Sustained, inclusive <b>economic growth</b>, full employment, decent work</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>9</b></td><td>Resilient <b>infrastructure</b>, sustainable industrialisation, innovation</td></tr>\n            </tbody>\n          </table>\n        "},{"title":"Goals 10–17","html":"\n          <table class=\"tbl\">\n            <tbody>\n              <tr><td><b>10</b></td><td>Reduce <b>inequality</b> within and among countries</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>11</b></td><td>Inclusive, safe, resilient, sustainable <b>cities</b></td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>12</b></td><td>Sustainable <b>consumption and production</b></td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>13</b></td><td>Urgent <b>climate action</b></td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>14</b></td><td><b>Life below water</b>: oceans, seas, marine resources</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>15</b></td><td><b>Life on land</b>: ecosystems, forests, desertification, land degradation, biodiversity loss</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>16</b></td><td><b>Peace, justice</b> and strong, accountable institutions</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>17</b></td><td><b>Partnerships</b>: means of implementation, global partnership</td></tr>\n            </tbody>\n          </table>\n        "},{"title":"Remembering them","html":"\n          <table class=\"tbl\">\n            <thead><tr><th>Group</th><th>Goals</th></tr></thead>\n            <tbody>\n              <tr><td>People (basic needs)</td><td>1 poverty, 2 hunger, 3 health, 4 education, 5 gender, 6 water</td></tr>\n              <tr><td>Prosperity</td><td>7 energy, 8 work, 9 infrastructure, 10 inequality, 11 cities, 12 consumption</td></tr>\n              <tr><td>Planet</td><td>13 climate, 14 water life, 15 land life</td></tr>\n              <tr><td>Peace and partnership</td><td>16 institutions, 17 partnerships</td></tr>\n            </tbody>\n          </table>\n          <div class=\"note heads-up\">Goal <b>6</b> is water and sanitation for people; Goal <b>14</b> is life in oceans and seas. Goal <b>13</b> is climate; Goal <b>15</b> covers forests and desertification.</div>\n        "}],"flashcards":[{"front":"How many SDGs are there?","back":"<b>17</b>."},{"front":"SDG 6?","back":"Clean <b>water and sanitation</b> for all."},{"front":"SDG 7?","back":"Affordable, clean <b>energy</b> for all."}],"cardCount":8,"formulaCount":0}],"figures":[]});
